<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Herm carriage ~ where a crossroads stands its gate, and how a vessel pulls through one

A public map crosses a wire only through a gate: the bare hop-by-hop route stands SHUT by name, and the
house named what opens it: an explicit Nexus, and a proven gate-native caller (the shut-routes house ruling, stable-founding-road #/rulings).
This module is both halves for a crossroads: where its floor gate stands, and the pull a vessel's carriage
dials through such gates.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/where`>>

!! Where ~ at the explicit Nexus, and only there

A herm stands a floor gate at a Nexus whose carriage board, ON ITS OWN REPLICA, counts a `carry` for its own
vessel key (`placeCarriedNexuses`, `via: "carrier-seal"`; `gateReadingsFor`). A charter it merely holds
stands no gate: holding A's charter is how a herm reads A's board, never a standing at A. A lararium stands
one at its own Nexus and at each it carries.

The explicit act that opens the herm relay (the shut-routes house ruling, stable-founding-road #/rulings) is the quorum's counted
carry over the herm's key. It travels to the herm by hand, because the membership relay ships SHUT by name
(`carry-bundle`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/how-it-answers`>>

!! How it answers ~ a herm answers the knock

A stood gate answers any PROVEN peer that knocked (operator ruling "A herm answers the knock"), read by the
vessel's one posture reader (`ownPlacePosture`, OPEN by class). The knock is the silence: only a peer handed
the gate key computes the path, and a bare route draws no upgrade. The carrying Nexus's charter posture
governs that Nexus's own hearths and never the waystone; `nexus posture` refuses on a herm by name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-pin-a-reader-dials`>>

!! The pin a reader dials

A herm's floor pin derives from its floor key, which no seat holds, and an announcement never
authenticates its own first pin (house ruling "The admit's gate pin"). So the herm signs ONE floor pin claim per
carrying Nexus, at the head of its own place KEL and with the signer the KEL seats there (the key the quorum's act names), and lays
the claim and its KEL rows on its own replica of that Nexus's carriage board (`layStatementOn`: once, and a claim at a new head lays
beside the older ones). A reader files the claim only where its own replica counts that signer as a carrier (`place-floor-pin`), and KEL
descent orders the claims it files; a rotated herm is carried again under its new signer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-a-reader-presents`>>

!! What a reader presents

`vesselCarriagePull` stands the pull the carriage cap is handed (`carriage-pull`). At each Nexus the vessel
stands in it presents, in this order, and composes nothing it does not hold:

# a PLACE carried there presents the quorum's counted `carry` over its own key, with its counted causal past
(the place arm, class `contracted`);
# a LARARIUM otherwise presents its worn face with the admit it took for that Nexus (`dial-presentation`).

A Nexus at which the vessel can present nothing is skipped by name (`presentation-absent`), never dialed
bare. A founder hearth presents its face at its own Nexus with the admit its own quorum lands for it
(`stable-founding-road`, the two-root witness: a founder self-admits), or its counted carry where it is
carried there as a place; a hearth that holds neither presents nothing there, and no bare face is composed.

<<~/ahu>>

